James wrote:
> Thomas Pornin <por...@bolet.org> wrote:
>
>> Usually, with a Samurai, I get Excalibur before Snickersnee.

As long as you are able to acquire a long sword.  With one it's easier
to get Excalibur.  Without one it's easier to get Snickersnee.  The
advantages of Excalibur for several classes of lawfuls make it worth
using as the primary melee weapon for an assortment of classes.

>> On the face of it, Excalibur is better: similar damage, but
>> also a +5 to-hit bonus which is very handy to compensate for
>> the two-weaponing malus, especially in the early stages of the
>> training.

The damage is very close between the two artifacts.  It's the other
differences tha tmatter the most.

> It also has auto-searching, which is a definite plus, especially
> if you don't have magic resistence, and want to avoid polymorph
> traps.

It's more than that.  Each enchantment improves the searching rate.  I
don't think you can get that even by wearing 2 rings of searching and
Excalibur does not give extra hunger for wielding it.  Gigantic
advantage.

> Also, I generally don't bother getting long sword above skilled
> before starting two-weaponing.

Expert is a tremendous bonus for missile combat.   Expert is a trivial
bonus for melee combat.


